    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test \u2014 the only test class in the project is `AcceptanceTest`, whose new `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` case passes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit following the codebase's existing `rejectIfXxx` reject-guard convention, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `rest/advice/DailyOwnerLimitException.java`: a small, cohesive class mirroring `CityAtCapacityException`. Its static `rejectIfAtLimit(existingOwners)` counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today and throws when the count reaches 100.\n\n**`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added one new `@ExceptionHandler` method mapping `DailyOwnerLimitException` to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429), identical in shape to the neighboring handlers (new method, no change to existing ones).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line invoking the guard (plus one import), placed alongside the existing `CityAtCapacity`/`DuplicateTelephone`/`DuplicateHousehold` checks so it runs before `saveOwner`.\n\nEach edited function stays simple (CC ~1, one changed line in the controller), and all new behaviour lives in a tiny standalone class with almost no surrounding complexity, so the WMC_other lever stays low.",
